From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/setup: constrain cryptography to 43.0.1

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 wheel availability: cryptography 43.0.0 has no riscv64 wheel, 43.0.1 is on pypi.riseproject.dev]

Pigweed's pip_install_pigweed_package target (pw_python_pip_install)
always installs the generated `pigweed` package with
--no-build-isolation, so every third-party dependency it pulls in that
has no wheel for the host is built inside the Pigweed venv itself.
cryptography==43.0.0 ships no riscv64 wheel on PyPI, so pip falls back
to its sdist, whose maturin build backend isn't in that venv
(ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'maturin'); building it would
also need a Rust toolchain the manylinux image doesn't have.

pypi.riseproject.dev ships cryptography 43.0.1 for riscv64
(cp39-abi3), a patch release whose only change is the OpenSSL version
compiled into the upstream wheels. Pin that version so the riscv64
build_wheels job can install it as a wheel. x86_64 (build_prepare)
gets 43.0.1 from PyPI just like 43.0.0.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 scripts/setup/constraints.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/setup/constraints.txt b/scripts/setup/constraints.txt
index 905ef7c..89cd541 100644
--- a/scripts/setup/constraints.txt
+++ b/scripts/setup/constraints.txt
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ contextlib2==21.6.0
     # via
     #   idf-component-manager
     #   schema
-cryptography==43.0.0
+cryptography==43.0.1
     # via
     #   -c constraints.esp32.txt
     #   -r requirements.all.txt
--
2.50.1
